# Starting and Stopping LocalStack

This section covers the basic commands used to start, check, and stop LocalStack.

No AWS services or resources are created in this process.

---

## 1. Start LocalStack

Start LocalStack with:

```bash
lstk start
```

This starts the LocalStack Docker container and makes the local AWS environment available.

### Check that it is running

```bash
docker ps
```

The LocalStack container should appear with a status similar to:

```text
Up ... (healthy)
```

---

## 2. Check LocalStack Health

To check whether LocalStack is responding:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:4566/_localstack/health
```

A working LocalStack installation will return information about the LocalStack environment and available AWS services.

---

## 3. View LocalStack Logs

To watch LocalStack logs:

```bash
lstk logs --follow
```

Press:

```text
Ctrl + C
```

to stop viewing the logs.

**Note:** `Ctrl + C` here only stops viewing the logs. It does not stop LocalStack.

---

## 4. Stop LocalStack

When finished working, stop LocalStack with:

```bash
lstk stop
```

This stops the LocalStack environment.

Check Docker:

```bash
docker ps
```

The LocalStack container should no longer appear among the running containers.

---

## 5. Start It Again

When you want to continue working another time:

```bash
lstk start
```

Then verify:

```bash
docker ps
```

---

# Basic Daily Workflow

### Starting your work

```bash
lstk start
```

Check:

```bash
docker ps
```

Work with LocalStack.

### Finishing your work

```bash
lstk stop
```

Check:

```bash
docker ps
```

---

# Quick Reference

| Action                  | Command                                         |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Start LocalStack        | `lstk start`                                    |
| Check Docker containers | `docker ps`                                     |
| Check LocalStack health | `curl http://127.0.0.1:4566/_localstack/health` |
| View logs               | `lstk logs --follow`                            |
| Stop viewing logs       | `Ctrl + C`                                      |
| Stop LocalStack         | `lstk stop`                                     |

## Simple Mental Model

```text
START
  │
  ▼
lstk start
  │
  ▼
Docker starts LocalStack
  │
  ▼
Local AWS environment is running
  │
  │
  │  Do your work
  │
  ▼
lstk stop
  │
  ▼
LocalStack stops
```

You can think of it as:

```text
lstk start  →  Turn the car on
              ↓
             Drive
              ↓
lstk stop   →  Turn the car off
```
